00:33:08.460 --> 00:33:34.940
Titan wasn't human.

00:33:34.940 --> 00:33:36.940
How's Lois?

00:33:36.940 --> 00:33:39.940
She's pretty banged up, but the doctor says she's going to be all right.

00:33:39.940 --> 00:33:40.940
She's already started my doctor.

00:33:40.940 --> 00:33:42.940
working on her article about the fight call.

00:33:42.940 --> 00:33:49.150
Don't worry, she didn't see me do anything news where they won't be making any headlines.

00:33:49.150 --> 00:33:52.150
I'm glad to know she's fine.

00:33:52.150 --> 00:33:54.150
How are you doing?

00:33:54.150 --> 00:34:00.650
I thought the Titan was the last prisoner I let escape from the Phantom Zone,

00:34:00.650 --> 00:34:06.519
looking at all of these.

00:34:06.519 --> 00:34:09.519
If there are any more out there, I'm sure you'll find them.

00:34:09.519 --> 00:34:12.659
Then what?

00:34:12.659 --> 00:34:18.739
I don't know how to return them to the Phantom Zone.

00:34:18.739 --> 00:34:22.739
The only way to get rid of them is to kill them like I did Titan.

00:34:22.739 --> 00:34:23.739
Clark.

00:34:23.739 --> 00:34:26.739
From what you told me, that was an accident.

00:34:26.739 --> 00:34:28.739
That's what I keep telling myself.

00:34:28.739 --> 00:34:31.739
Well, what if it wasn't? He would have killed you.

00:34:31.739 --> 00:34:33.739
So I just killed him first?

00:34:33.739 --> 00:34:36.739
How does that make me any different than Titan?

00:34:36.739 --> 00:34:40.739
What you're feeling right now is what makes you different.

00:34:40.739 --> 00:34:47.739
Regret, remorse for a vicious creature who would have murdered you and Lois without a second thought?

00:34:47.739 --> 00:34:52.739
Those feelings are what make you human, no matter how much you deny it.

00:34:52.739 --> 00:34:55.690
And what about the anger?

00:34:55.690 --> 00:34:59.320
I wanted to kill him, Mom.

00:34:59.320 --> 00:35:02.320
I wanted to kill him with my bare hands.

00:35:02.320 --> 00:35:06.429
I never felt raised like that before.

00:35:06.429 --> 00:35:10.780
You were angry before you ever heard of Titan.

00:35:10.780 --> 00:35:13.780
We both know that's not what this is about.

00:35:13.780 --> 00:35:27.650
How could she marry Lex?

00:35:27.650 --> 00:35:30.960
No, Clark, but she made her choice.

00:35:30.960 --> 00:35:35.619
Or someone made it for her.

00:35:35.619 --> 00:35:41.869
I have to figure out what happened. I gotta do something.

00:35:41.869 --> 00:35:45.869
Honey, I understand how much this hurts.

00:35:45.869 --> 00:35:49.869
But part of being human, of being in love,

00:35:49.869 --> 00:35:54.789
in love is learning to let go.

00:35:54.789 --> 00:36:00.900
If you can't, I'm afraid the anger you're feeling will always be there.

00:36:00.900 --> 00:36:34.019
Now called. I wanted to know if you'd like some company tomorrow.

00:36:34.019 --> 00:36:35.019
I don't know.

00:36:35.019 --> 00:36:42.409
Lana, you haven't left this room since we got back from the hospital.

00:36:42.409 --> 00:36:48.280
I like it here.

00:36:48.280 --> 00:36:53.690
Called Dr. Langston to tell him what happened.

00:36:53.690 --> 00:36:55.690
He told me he was killed in a car accident.

00:36:55.690 --> 00:37:19.840
Day of our wedding. Why is all this happening?

00:37:19.840 --> 00:37:22.840
Things in life are just out of your control.

00:37:22.840 --> 00:37:39.860
control. Sometimes you have to live in the hands of greater power.

00:37:39.860 --> 00:37:54.090
I'm so sorry. I have to know for sure.

00:37:54.090 --> 00:37:58.780
I need to get my files from Dr. Langston's office.

00:37:58.780 --> 00:38:13.809
How can I help make the pain go away?

00:38:13.809 --> 00:39:04.960
And forget you ever heard of Lana Luther.

